2025-05-01 02:41:02 - Thread-924 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant tables / columns and why they matter  
• `prod.CytoConverted.RefNo` / `CaseNo` / `InvNo` / `Clone` –‐ clone identifiers to be matched across the three required chromosome events.  
• `prod.CytoConverted.ChrOrd` –‐ numeric chromosome (13, 17, 11).  
• `prod.CytoConverted.Start`, `prod.CytoConverted.End` –‐ genomic coordinates to test whether the event covers (or at least overlaps) the requested interval.  
• `prod.CytoConverted.Type` –‐ tells whether the segment is a ‘Loss’ or a ‘Gain’.  
• `prod.KaryClone.RefNo` / `CaseNo` / `InvNo` / `CloneNo` –‐ clone identifiers that match the CytoConverted rows.  
• `prod.KaryClone.CloneShort` –‐ short karyotype string to be returned in the final output.

Main filtering conditions  
1. Loss on chr13 that spans 48 303 751 – 48 481 890 → `ChrOrd = 13` AND `Type = 'Loss'` AND `Start <= 48 303 751` AND `End >= 48 481 890` (or the more permissive overlap test `Start <= 48 481 890 AND End >= 48 303 751`).  
2. Loss on chr17 that spans 7 668 421 – 7 687 490 → `ChrOrd = 17` AND `Type = 'Loss'` AND analogous range test.  
3. Gain on chr11 that spans 108 223 067 – 108 369 102 → `ChrOrd = 11` AND `Type = 'Gain'` AND analogous range test.

Below are ten exploratory → increasingly complex BigQuery SQL statements (all limited to 20 rows) finishing with a complete answer query.

```sql
-- 1. Preview a handful of CytoConverted entries
SELECT *
FROM `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Look at chr13 losses only
SELECT DISTINCT RefNo, CaseNo, InvNo, Clone, ChrOrd, Start, End
FROM `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted`
WHERE ChrOrd = 13
  AND Type = 'Loss'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. chr13 losses that cover the 48.3–48.4 Mb interval
SELECT DISTINCT RefNo, CaseNo, InvNo, Clone, Start, End
FROM `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted`
WHERE ChrOrd = 13
  AND Type = 'Loss'
  AND Start <= 48303751
  AND End   >= 48481890
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. chr17 losses that cover the 7.66–7.69 Mb interval
SELECT DISTINCT RefNo, CaseNo, InvNo, Clone, Start, End
FROM `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted`
WHERE ChrOrd = 17
  AND Type = 'Loss'
  AND Start <= 7668421
  AND End   >= 7687490
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. chr11 gains that cover the 108.22–108.37 Mb interval
SELECT DISTINCT RefNo, CaseNo, InvNo, Clone, Start, End
FROM `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted`
WHERE ChrOrd = 11
  AND Type = 'Gain'
  AND Start <= 108223067
  AND End   >= 108369102
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Clones that have BOTH the chr13‑loss AND the chr17‑loss criteria
SELECT DISTINCT c13.RefNo, c13.CaseNo, c13.InvNo, c13.Clone
FROM `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS c13
JOIN `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS c17
  USING (RefNo, CaseNo, InvNo, Clone)
WHERE c13.ChrOrd = 13 AND c13.Type = 'Loss'
  AND c13.Start <= 48303751 AND c13.End >= 48481890
  AND c17.ChrOrd = 17 AND c17.Type = 'Loss'
  AND c17.Start <= 7668421  AND c17.End >= 7687490
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Clones that satisfy chr13‑loss, chr17‑loss, AND chr11‑gain
SELECT DISTINCT c13.RefNo, c13.CaseNo, c13.InvNo, c13.Clone
FROM `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS c13
JOIN `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS c17
  USING (RefNo, CaseNo, InvNo, Clone)
JOIN `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS c11
  USING (RefNo, CaseNo, InvNo, Clone)
WHERE c13.ChrOrd = 13 AND c13.Type = 'Loss'
  AND c13.Start <= 48303751 AND c13.End >= 48481890
  AND c17.ChrOrd = 17 AND c17.Type = 'Loss'
  AND c17.Start <= 7668421  AND c17.End >= 7687490
  AND c11.ChrOrd = 11 AND c11.Type = 'Gain'
  AND c11.Start <= 108223067 AND c11.End >= 108369102
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Same as #7 but also pull the three segment rows side‑by‑side
SELECT DISTINCT
  c13.RefNo, c13.CaseNo, c13.InvNo, c13.Clone,
  c13.ChrOrd   AS Chr13_ChrOrd, c13.Start AS Chr13_Start, c13.End AS Chr13_End,
  c17.ChrOrd   AS Chr17_ChrOrd, c17.Start AS Chr17_Start, c17.End AS Chr17_End,
  c11.ChrOrd   AS Chr11_ChrOrd, c11.Start AS Chr11_Start, c11.End AS Chr11_End
FROM `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS c13
JOIN `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS c17
  USING (RefNo, CaseNo, InvNo, Clone)
JOIN `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS c11
  USING (RefNo, CaseNo, InvNo, Clone)
WHERE c13.ChrOrd = 13 AND c13.Type = 'Loss'
  AND c13.Start <= 48303751 AND c13.End >= 48481890
  AND c17.ChrOrd = 17 AND c17.Type = 'Loss'
  AND c17.Start <= 7668421  AND c17.End >= 7687490
  AND c11.ChrOrd = 11 AND c11.Type = 'Gain'
  AND c11.Start <= 108223067 AND c11.End >= 108369102
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Add the short karyotype string from KaryClone
SELECT DISTINCT
  c13.RefNo, c13.CaseNo, c13.InvNo, c13.Clone AS CloneNo,
  c13.ChrOrd AS Chr13_ChrOrd, c13.Start AS Chr13_Start, c13.End AS Chr13_End,
  c17.ChrOrd AS Chr17_ChrOrd, c17.Start AS Chr17_Start, c17.End AS Chr17_End,
  c11.ChrOrd AS Chr11_ChrOrd, c11.Start AS Chr11_Start, c11.End AS Chr11_End,
  k.CloneShort
FROM `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS c13
JOIN `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS c17
  USING (RefNo, CaseNo, InvNo, Clone)
JOIN `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS c11
  USING (RefNo, CaseNo, InvNo, Clone)
LEFT JOIN `mitelman-db.prod.KaryClone` AS k
  ON k.RefNo   = c13.RefNo
 AND k.CaseNo  = c13.CaseNo
 AND k.InvNo   = c13.InvNo
 AND k.CloneNo = c13.Clone
WHERE c13.ChrOrd = 13 AND c13.Type = 'Loss'
  AND c13.Start <= 48303751 AND c13.End >= 48481890
  AND c17.ChrOrd = 17 AND c17.Type = 'Loss'
  AND c17.Start <= 7668421  AND c17.End >= 7687490
  AND c11.ChrOrd = 11 AND c11.Type = 'Gain'
  AND c11.Start <= 108223067 AND c11.End >= 108369102
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL ANSWER: distinct clones fulfilling all three criteria,
--     with chromosomal details for each region plus the CloneShort karyotype.
SELECT DISTINCT
  c13.RefNo         AS RefNo,
  c13.CaseNo        AS CaseNo,
  c13.InvNo         AS InvNo,
  c13.Clone         AS CloneNo,
  -- chr13 loss segment
  c13.ChrOrd        AS Chr13_ChrOrd,
  c13.Start         AS Chr13_Start,
  c13.End           AS Chr13_End,
  -- chr17 loss segment
  c17.ChrOrd        AS Chr17_ChrOrd,
  c17.Start         AS Chr17_Start,
  c17.End           AS Chr17_End,
  -- chr11 gain segment
  c11.ChrOrd        AS Chr11_ChrOrd,
  c11.Start         AS Chr11_Start,
  c11.End           AS Chr11_End,
  -- karyotype
  k.CloneShort      AS Karyotype_Short
FROM `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS c13
JOIN `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS c17
  USING (RefNo, CaseNo, InvNo, Clone)
JOIN `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS c11
  USING (RefNo, CaseNo, InvNo, Clone)
LEFT JOIN `mitelman-db.prod.KaryClone` AS k
  ON k.RefNo   = c13.RefNo
 AND k.CaseNo  = c13.CaseNo
 AND k.InvNo   = c13.InvNo
 AND k.CloneNo = c13.Clone
WHERE -- chr13 loss covering 48 303 751‑48 481 890
      c13.ChrOrd = 13 AND c13.Type = 'Loss'
  AND c13.Start <= 48303751
  AND c13.End   >= 48481890
  -- chr17 loss covering 7 668 421‑7 687 490
  AND c17.ChrOrd = 17 AND c17.Type = 'Loss'
  AND c17.Start <= 7668421
  AND c17.End   >= 7687490
  -- chr11 gain covering 108 223 067‑108 369 102
  AND c11.ChrOrd = 11 AND c11.Type = 'Gain'
  AND c11.Start <= 108223067
  AND c11.End   >= 108369102
ORDER BY RefNo, CaseNo, InvNo, CloneNo
LIMIT 20;
```
