Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant tables / columns and why they matter  
• `prod.CytoConverted.RefNo` / `CaseNo` / `InvNo` / `Clone` –‐ clone identifiers to be matched across the three required chromosome events.  
• `prod.CytoConverted.ChrOrd` –‐ numeric chromosome (13, 17, 11).  
• `prod.CytoConverted.Start`, `prod.CytoConverted.End` –‐ genomic coordinates to test whether the event covers (or at least overlaps) the requested interval.  
• `prod.CytoConverted.Type` –‐ tells whether the segment is a ‘Loss’ or a ‘Gain’.  
• `prod.KaryClone.RefNo` / `CaseNo` / `InvNo` / `CloneNo` –‐ clone identifiers that match the CytoConverted rows.  
• `prod.KaryClone.CloneShort` –‐ short karyotype string to be returned in the final output.

Main filtering conditions  
1. Loss on chr13 that spans 48 303 751 – 48 481 890 → `ChrOrd = 13` AND `Type = 'Loss'` AND `Start <= 48 303 751` AND `End >= 48 481 890` (or the more permissive overlap test `Start <= 48 481 890 AND End >= 48 303 751`).  
2. Loss on chr17 that spans 7 668 421 – 7 687 490 → `ChrOrd = 17` AND `Type = 'Loss'` AND analogous range test.  
3. Gain on chr11 that spans 108 223 067 – 108 369 102 → `ChrOrd = 11` AND `Type = 'Gain'` AND analogous range test.

